xnu 0490: read the QCA6490 PBL log before the BHI windows

Measured 2026-11-27: 0489 reaches the boot-ROM authentication stage
(`TCSR_PBL_LOGGING=0xef0a0111`) and the `PBL_BOOTSTRAP_STATUS` read then
hangs the AHB window before the PBL log SRAM is read. Read the log first,
drop the two registers that hang, and add the two error-debug words the hang
had kept out. The same boot dumps the image's ELF header, program headers
and hash-segment words from host memory, so a wrong or corrupted file names
itself: the donor `amss20.bin` has `e_entry=0x1436500`, `e_phoff=0x34`,
`e_phentsize=32` and 17 program headers.

